<item>
            <title>[JGVT-3610] Balance Interface: Auto-check the neg property in Preparations Sub Table - updated Story JGVT-1711</title>
                <link>https://jira.jnj.com/browse/JGVT-3610</link>
                <project id="46901" key="JGVT">TDS - Revvity Signals ELN</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#172b4d&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;As a User performing weighing&lt;/b&gt;,&#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;font color=&quot;#172b4d&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;I want&lt;/b&gt;&#160;the System to show the absolute value of the difference in weight in the preparation Sub Table when the Original value retrieved from the Balance Interface was negative, and show the raw date (the negative weight) in the Balance data interface&#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;font color=&quot;#172b4d&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;So that&lt;/b&gt; I can easily see that the raw data shows a negative weigh, but work with absolute values in my preparations&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#172b4d&quot;&gt;Technical Design&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#172b4d&quot;&gt;Actual weight&#160; is either the saved value or the display value and should be positive&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#172b4d&quot;&gt;stored value and displayed value will both be the absolute value&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#172b4d&quot;&gt;Update code to remove the negative column checkbox&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#172b4d&quot;&gt;Confirm it works on Both the DEV and GMP Template.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Testing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Need to coordinate so that the balance reads a negative value. Let Pascal know 1 day before testing so that someone is on site near the balance.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Needs to confirm that this works for both the GxP-DEV and GxP-GMP General Templates.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
